{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794738313,"nonce":"5s9iC6u0rKAGpFWIEIriLpTEl90=","message":"TAST format 2 and our own metadata (15ea0aa1). Answers the audit's list of gaps; the oracle against the Haxe exporter still matches on the unit suite (8902 functions, only the build-date constant differs).\n\nNew in the file (all written by the plugin; the Haxe exporter writes the sections empty and is now legacy):\n- Order: the types as `com.types` lists them, which is the static-initialization order. A class that is not listed is only referenced.\n- `init_func` on a class: its `__init__` block, as a function.\n- Field flags NOT_PHYSICAL, EXTERN and DYNAMIC; `opt_mask` on function types (bit i = argument i is optional), which is part of type identity because an optional non-nullable argument is passed by reference.\n- A type parameter's constraints, in the class record's interface list.\n- Metas: declaration metadata on classes, fields, enums, enum constructors, abstracts and locals, with arguments as nodes (constants, identifiers with dotted paths, arrays, objects). Expression metadata (`TMeta`) now carries its arguments after the expression.\n- `meta_root` on classes and enums: the runtime metadata object that `Texpr.build_metadata` builds, as an expression, for the reflection API.\n- Defines (all of them: hl-ver, debug, user flags) and Resources (name and bytes; sorted by name, since genhl's order is a Hashtbl fold).\n\nOur own metadata, as the direct path's input:\n- Namespace `:ash.*`, compile-time only. A name with a colon never enters the runtime metadata object, so it cannot change reflection.\n- Exported: every `:ash.*` entry, plus the names genhl reads (`:hlNative`, `:struct`, `:packed`, `:coreType`, `:realPath`, `:noExpr`). The HL names stay because the HL std binds natives with them and the runtime ABI is HashLink's. One predicate, `exported_meta` in tast_export.ml, decides.\n- The vocabulary is not fixed. Each name lands with the pass that reads it (final and closed-world receivers, no-throw, non-null, purity, bounds, hot and cold, layout), as in decision 3.\n- Where it can sit: on a declaration (`@:ash.noThrow function f()`), on a variable (`var @:ash.keep x`), or on an expression (`@:ash.unchecked a[i]`).\n- Constraint: the typer drops metadata on an expression it does not know unless the build defines `retain-untyped-meta`. Init macros run after the typer is created, so the plugin cannot set it; it warns when the define is missing, and the `ash` driver has to pass it. Declaration metadata is always kept. `@:ash.keep var x` puts the metadata on the expression, not on the variable.\n- Prebuilt HL bytecode has none of this. The HL frontend keeps working unchanged, and the lowering treats a missing hint as the conservative case.\n\nSize: unit suite after filters, 2763 class records, 328k nodes, 10.7 MB, build 236 ms in the plugin on the Mac (was 9.9 MB before these sections: 15174 metadata entries, 2619 order entries, 3 resources, 26 defines). tast_dump prints the new section sizes.\n\nStill open in the exporter: overloads, and 7 typedefs that expand without bound are cut at depth 8 (same in both writers). Next: the Rust crate that builds the whole-program tables (overrides, virtual slots, type tables, pools) from this file.","files":null}]}